  "arguments": {}
}
```

blocks.wait_for_approval:
- **{{ref:needs}}:** {{ref:needsNothing}}
- **{{ref:hints}}:** {{ref:readOnly}} · {{ref:idempotent}}
- **{{ref:household}}:** {{ref:householdAdmin}}

**{{ref:description}}**

```text
Wait for approvals this access key created instead of polling get_approval_status. Pass the required approval_ids list, including for one approval. Collect confirm-gated calls first, then wait once for the whole set; the operator may resolve them in any order or batch. Already-resolved approvals return immediately; others wait for approval, rejection or expiry, up to the server-capped timeout. The response includes every status and outstanding ID. On timeout, unresolved approvals stay pending and you may wait again. Results contain result_is_error and clipped result_text; short failure messages remain intact. Use get_approval_status with one approval_id for its full result.
```

**{{ref:parameters}}**

```text
approval_ids: array<string> [1.. items]  (required)
  Several approval_ids to wait for together. Use instead of approval_id after a run of confirm-gated calls.
timeout: integer
  Max seconds to wait (capped by the server). Default is the server cap.
```

**{{ref:example}}**

```json
{
  "name": "wait_for_approval",
  "arguments": {
    "approval_ids": [
      "apr_01JD4R7T8Y9U0I1O2P3A4S5D6F"
    ],
    "timeout": 120
  }
}
```

