```text
Create a new Home Assistant script in scripts.yaml, which configuration.yaml must load with a plain !include; any other layout is refused. Adding a call to shell_command, python_script, pyscript, hassio or rest_command, a restart, stop or update.install, a templated action name, or a blueprint always needs an administrator's approval, even with this capability on Allow. Provide a unique script_id slug (e.g. 'morning_routine'). HA validates before saving; invalid configs are rejected with an error. To build from a blueprint instead, pass 'use_blueprint' ({'path': ..., 'input': {...}}) in place of 'sequence'; see list_blueprints. Returns a receipt with config, write_success, reload_status and registration (status, observed entity_id and state_present). A registration timeout does not undo the saved write; retry a lookup, not the write.
