**{{ref:description}}**

```text
Replace the configuration of an existing Home Assistant script. The 'config' object ENTIRELY replaces the current script configuration, so call get_script first and resend every part you want to keep; anything you omit is destroyed. Only entries written inline in scripts.yaml can be changed; one defined in hand-written YAML, an included file or a package is refused. A config holding !secret or !include text cannot be written. Adding a call to shell_command, python_script, pyscript, hassio or rest_command, a restart, stop or update.install, a templated action name, or a blueprint always needs an administrator's approval, even with this capability on Allow. Returns the updated configuration. The config is validated by HA before saving - invalid configs are rejected with an error. Use the script_id storage key from list_scripts; a renamed entity_id may have a different suffix. Returns a receipt with config, write_success, reload_status and registration (status, observed entity_id and state_present). A registration timeout does not undo the saved write; retry a lookup, not the write.
```

**{{ref:parameters}}**

```text
script_id: string  (required)
